# Codex permission rules. Tracked deliberately: an untracked allow-list is per-machine.
# Read-only and hermetic only. Mutating commands are absent and fall through to a prompt.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-31 after review. Every defect below was the same mistake: a comment
# asserting an invariant that POSITIONAL PREFIX MATCHING CANNOT ENFORCE. A rule can only
# constrain a command's PREFIX -- never a flag or refspec that appears later in argv.
# If you cannot express the safe subset as a prefix, do not write the allow.
#
# NOT a blanket allow. A blanket `just` auto-approves every recipe the justfile gains later,
# and an agent that can edit the justfile can run anything through it. The earlier claim that
# a blanket 'stays correct as recipes are added rather than going stale' was exactly backwards.
# Enumerated hermetic recipes only. RE-CHECK this list when a recipe is added.
prefix_rule(pattern=["just", ["audit", "docs-build", "fmt", "fmt-check", "lint", "test", "test-doc", "test-prop"]], decision="allow")
